 35CL c  {+37}Cl|){+35}Cl+2n from J|p=3/2+ {+37}Cl ground state.                
 35CL c  1971Vi02: A 40-MeV proton beam was produced from the Grenoble variable 
 35CL2c  energy cyclotron at intensities of 20-200 nA depending on the          
 35CL3c  scattering angle with a 90-keV energy resolution. Targets were natural 
 35CL4c  purified chlorine gas 100 mm in diameter and 25 mm in height and solid 
 35CL5c  AgCl of isotopic {+37}Cl. The reaction particles were detected using   
 35CL6c  two separate counter telescopes consisting of a 200-|mm                
 35CL7c  phosphorous-drifted silicon |DE detector, a 3-mm lithium-drifted       
 35CL8c  silicon E detector, and a 3-mm lithium-drifted silicon E-reject        
 35CL9c  detector with FWHM=130 keV for tritons. Measured |s(E{-t},|q). Deduced 
 35CLAc  L-transfers for 7 levels from zero-range Nelson spin-dependent-DWBA    
 35CLBc  analysis of the measured |s(|q).                                       
 35CL c  2017Ch22: a 30-MeV proton beam was produced from the Holifield         
 35CL2c  Radioactive Ion Beam Facility at Oak Ridge National Laboratory. The    
 35CL3c  target was |J600 |mg PbCl{-2} (|J95% enriched and |J160 |mg/cm{+2} in  
 35CL4c  {+37}Cl) on a 20 |mg/cm{+2} parylene (C{-8}H{-8}) backing. Tritons were
 35CL5c  detected using the annular silicon detector array (SIDAR) consisting of
 35CL6c  100-|mm-|DE and 1000|mm-E telescopes with FWHM=60-100 keV. Measured    
 35CL7c  |s(E{-t},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, and L-transfers from TWOFNR-DWBA  
 35CL8c  analysis of the measured |s(|q). Provided the first spin-parity        
 35CL9c  constraint of a 306-keV {+34}S(p,|g) resonance potentially important   
 35CLAc  for nova nucleosynthesis.                                              
 35CL c  Other: 1985Mi06.                                                       
